{"seq":null,"source_sha256":"d45730ae8512188e03d768ea37c4e43f8854f82ab91b2b1610a027ac4aee5734","commit_to":{"owner":"teamwork-inc-test","repo":"e2e-team-repo","branch":"main"},"doc_stem":"2026-10-10-2-e2e-default-ref-1791624510917","status":"completed","machine":{"spec_version":8,"spec_hash":"48411dad1f94"},"checkpoint":"navigate","run_id":"mp-eng-7a1c675d","payload":{"expand_iris":[],"focus":"Tanya TeamOwner testing that omitting a ref creates a topic branch; default-ref behavior and topic branch creation","rationale":"The map exposes only the Anti-Slack positioning narrative, while the document is solely a test of omitted-ref topic-branch behavior; these themes do not overlap. I checked the thematic, document, people, and unplaced doors: the two listed documents concern context preservation and real-time chat, there are no people groups or unplaced positions, and no surfaced position or narrative bears on this test. I therefore deliberately expanded no content.","n8n_execution_id":"159370","expansion_count":0,"context":"# Perspective — teamwork-inc-test/e2e-team-repo @ c2a43aa67fa1c7ae8b807a146140f146543d5105\npin: ac168ed96e2811e59f8c7da03e411ff9b641df2e\n\nSections: (1) THE MAP — this graph's richest ground, full narration; (2) COVERAGE — what's active, contested, unplaced, and quiet across everything else, meaning inside whisper-brackets; (3) DOORS — complete axes (areas, people, dimensions, documents, unplaced), each one expand away; (4) FOCUS — material loaded for your focus, LAST. The map, coverage, and doors never vary with your focus.\n\n^-marked entries are compressed stubs carrying child addresses. Their narration and any surfaced witness quotes are verbatim-accurate — quote them as-is — but a stub carries no provenance (source, date, supersession). Expand (aswritten_expand with the IRIs you need) before any claim that turns on WHEN or by WHOM something was said, or whether it is still the current framing. Witness-depth sections below already carry full provenance.\n\nThis entry is BOUNDED — the whole graph is deliberately not inlined. Every node is reachable within a bounded number of expands: before concluding the perspective is silent on your subject, check the map and coverage, then expand the door whose axis would hold it (^Thematic for topics and areas, ^People for anyone, ^Documents for a call or memory, ^Unplaced for loose positions). Absence becomes signal only after the relevant door shows nothing.\n\n# The map — this graph's richest ground (top fidelity band)\n\n## ^Narrative_AntiSlackPositioning  [4 children · 20260310]\nTanya frames the product against Slack's real-time model. The anti-Slack label is the primary positioning thesis: every conversation should produce a persistent decision artifact.\n  decisions-under 1 · evidence 4 — expand ^Narrative_AntiSlackPositioning for the full child index\n\n# Coverage — narrated, from four directions\n\nActive: [ Position_ContextPreservationNextSprint · Next sprint focus: context preservation — linking decisions to t… ^Position_ContextPreservationNextSprint ] · [ Position_AntiPatternRealtimeChat · Real-time chat (Slack, Teams) is the named anti-pattern. The pro… ^Position_AntiPatternRealtimeChat ] — the newest witnessed work, one document each.\n\n# Doors — pick an axis\n\n[ ^Thematic — every area (0) by name ] [ ^People 0 ] [ ^Dimensions — 0 axes ] [ ^Documents 2 ] [ ^Unplaced 0 ]\nEach door expands to a complete axis: aswritten_expand(iris=[\"Thematic\"]) — same coords as this perspective. Nothing in the graph is outside every door.\n\n# Focus: Tanya TeamOwner testing that omitting a ref creates a topic branch; default-ref behavior and topic branch creation (witness depth — per-call section)\n\n### Position_Sprint4ThesisProven\ntype: Position\nwitnessed: 20260322\nsource: Sample_Sprint4Retro_20260322\nTanya: 'This sprint proved the thesis.' The widget intercepts the moment of consensus in any chat thread and creates a persistent decision record with full context, requiring zero extra steps.\nunder: PositioningThesis, Narrative_ZeroEffortCapture\n\n### Position_ProductCategoryAsyncPlatform\ntype: Position\nwitnessed: 20260310\nsource: Sample_TeamworkProductVision_20260310\nProduct category explicitly defined as 'Structured async decision platform' — a deliberate category creation move against real-time chat tools.\nunder: Narrative_AntiSlackPositioning\n\n### Narrative_AntiSlackPositioning\ntype: Narrative\nwitnessed: 20260310\nsource: Sample_TeamworkProductVision_20260310\nTanya frames the product against Slack's real-time model. The anti-Slack label is the primary positioning thesis: every conversation should produce a persistent decision artifact.\nTeamwork Inc positions itself as the anti-Slack: structured async decisions over real-time noise\nunder: PositioningThesis\n\n### Obs_TanyaAntiSlackQuote\ntype: Observation\nwitnessed: 20260310\nsource: Sample_TeamworkProductVision_20260310\nTanya's verbatim framing of the anti-Slack positioning thesis.\nunder: PositioningThesis\n\n### Position_WebhookArchitecture\ntype: Position\nwitnessed: 20260322\nsource: Sample_Sprint4Retro_20260322\nArchitecture decision: event-driven capture via webhook, not polling. Tanya: 'Polling would kill us at scale. Webhooks mean we only process actual decisions, not every message.'\nunder: StackOverview, Narrative_ZeroEffortCapture\n\n### StyleObs_Sprint4_DirectQuote\ntype: StyleObservation\nwitnessed: 20260322\nsource: Sample_Sprint4Retro_20260322\ntrue\nDocument uses direct first-person quotes from named executives (Tanya, Tina) to anchor every key decision. Quotes are attributed inline with speaker name and colon.\n> \"This sprint proved the thesis. The widget intercepts the moment someone says 'let's go with option B'\"\nunder: ToneDirectPersonal\n\n### Sample_Sprint4Retro_20260322\ntype: Sample\nwitnessed: 20260322\nSprint retrospective for the async decision widget feature. Participants: Tanya Owner (CEO), Tina Teammate (Head of Product), Dev Team. Covers shipped feature, key decisions, and blockers resolved.\nSprint 4 Retro: Async Decision Widget\n\n### Obs_TanyaThesisProven\ntype: Observation\nwitnessed: 20260322\nsource: Sample_Sprint4Retro_20260322\nTanya confirms the product thesis is validated by Sprint 4 delivery: zero-extra-step decision capture at the moment of consensus.\nunder: PositioningThesis\n","positions":"","pin":"ac168ed96e2811e59f8c7da03e411ff9b641df2e","positions_consult":"{\"positions\":[]}","context_bytes":5253},"live_run_id":"a0fc5f962e8e","at":"2026-10-10T09:28:52Z"}
